hich is more available (2 left) compared to W3 (1 left). This sets up potential for multiple chows and a valid hand.\nReason: Waiting for T4 (2 remaining) is more favorable than waiting for W3 (1 remaining). Forming the T2-T3-T4 chow would complement the existing B1-B2-B3 chow and potential W1-W2-W3 chow, maximizing meld opportunities.\nAnswer: Play T3"}
